WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.245
Certificate validation failures should fail safely or follow a documented
secure error path.

2
00:00:05.245 --> 00:00:11.474
A hostname mismatch, expired certificate, untrusted issuer, or purpose
mismatch is not just an inconvenience.

3
00:00:11.474 --> 00:00:15.145
It means the client cannot confirm the trust decision it expected.

4
00:00:15.145 --> 00:00:25.177
User-facing errors should be limited and clear, while internal logs can
capture safe diagnostic detail for operators without exposing secrets or
sensitive certificate material.

5
00:00:25.177 --> 00:00:28.979
Logging should make validation observable without becoming a leak.

6
00:00:28.979 --> 00:00:38.159
Useful fields include service name, environment, safe error category,
validation outcome, certificate expiration warning, dependency name, and
correlation ID.

7
00:00:38.159 --> 00:00:44.781
Logs should avoid private keys, tokens, credentials, full sensitive
payloads, and unnecessary certificate details.

8
00:00:44.781 --> 00:00:51.730
Structured logging helps teams monitor trends and investigate incidents
without dumping raw internals to broad audiences.

9
00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:54.353
Testing should cover expected trust behavior.

10
00:00:54.353 --> 00:01:04.712
Tests can verify hostname mismatch handling, expired or untrusted
certificate behavior at a high level, development versus production
settings, and safe errors when validation fails.

11
00:01:04.712 --> 00:01:16.317
Dependency and library review should confirm that clients, drivers,
runtimes, and container images use maintained TLS behavior and that
validation exceptions do not creep into shared production code paths.

12
00:01:16.317 --> 00:01:19.595
Monitoring and incident response complete the lifecycle.

13
00:01:19.595 --> 00:01:27.004
Teams should monitor certificate expiration, handshake failures,
validation errors, renewal failures, and configuration drift.

14
00:01:27.004 --> 00:01:41.428
If a private key is exposed, a certificate is misissued, or unsafe
validation settings are discovered, incident response should identify
affected services, rotate or revoke material as appropriate, review logs,
fix configuration, and add regression tests.

15
00:01:41.428 --> 00:01:46.280
Certificate validation must remain observable without weakening the trust
decision.
